H. Observation: 
•	Kruskal’s algorithm always considers the smallest-weight edge first. 
•	An edge is added only when it does not form a cycle. 
•	The Disjoint Set Union (DSU) efficiently detects cycles. 
•	For a graph with N vertices, the MST contains exactly N − 1 edges. 
•	The final sum of the selected edge weights gives the minimum spanning tree weight. 
•	The time complexity is approximately O(M log M) because the edges are sorted by weight. 



